    ex:sourceSummary "Dabaru is a 2024 Indian Bengali-language biographical sports drama film directed by Pathikrit Basu. Produced by Nandita Roy and Shiboprosad Mukherjee under the banner of Windows Production, the film is based on the life of the Indian chess Grandmaster Surya Shekhar Ganguly. The film chronicles the journey of Ganguly from North Kolkata's slums to becoming India's youngest Grandmaster at age 19, played by Arghya Basu Roy. It also features an ensemble cast of Dipankar De, Chiranjeet Chakraborty, Rituparna Sengupta, Shankar Chakraborty and Kaushik Sen in another pivotal roles." ;
